`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Candidate identity:"})," requested purpose, original prompt, generation/retrieval source, model/checkpoint, seed, source license and immutable asset hashes. Retain failures and candidates rejected before rendering."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Evidence packet:"})," camera extrinsics/intrinsics, units/up/front conventions, lighting/material setup, frame order, image sizes/crops and actual model-facing packet. Preserve original files separately from resized judge images."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Separate judgments:"})," semantic fit, visual coherence, geometric constraints, functional representation, runtime behavior and legal eligibility. Aesthetic ranking must not override a required collision, articulation, readability or rights gate."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Selection policy:"})," first acceptable, scalar ranker, sequential tournament and regenerate-with-revised-prompt are different algorithms. Declare pool size, tie rule, abstention, retries, judge repeats and candidate ordering."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Final independence:"})," use held-out views, target-engine state assertions and human checks where appropriate. Do not train, select and report solely against the same learned/VLM score. Block benchmark solutions and final-test evidence from reflective memory."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Budget and end state:"})," account for generator, renderer, evaluator, repair and infrastructure cost. Record accepted, rejected, inconclusive, infrastructure-failed and budget-exhausted separately. A rendered preview or saved scene is not proof of a functioning game."]}),`
`]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The most defensible first fixture is ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"selection over an already frozen, rights-cleared candidate pool"}),". It tests ranking/feedback without confounding generation quality, incurring paid generation calls, or suggesting that this source review granted execution permission. A later generation-in-the-loop study is a separate experiment."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["For dialogue drafts, the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/production-research-notes/#dialogue-drafting-preserve-preference-edited-acceptance-and-character-references",children:"Ubisoft authoring research"})," provides a separate example of why pairwise preference, edited acceptance, character-reference revisions and automatic style scores need distinct records. It does not establish a deployed visual-asset selection method."]}),`
